Linux gen-data prompt attribution and license notices

internal/core/gendata_prompt_linux.go adapts the reached semantics of
io-console 0.9.4 ext/io/console/console.c (set_noecho, set_rawmode,
ttymode and console_getch) and Ruby 3.4.9 io.c (io_getc), with the
UTF-8 prefix conditions of enc/utf_8.c. Original distributions:
https://github.com/ruby/io-console
https://github.com/ruby/ruby/tree/v3_4_9

This port selects the 2-clause BSDL option offered by io-console/Ruby
COPYING. The complete original BSDL follows below. The additional applicable
UTF-8/Onigmo copyright, conditions and disclaimers are retained separately.
No claim that every Ruby file shares one license is made.

Named modifications: use one borrowed original Linux input and retained Go
bufio.Reader; select the explicit alternative raw mask followed by intr:true;
perform one stable-descriptor setup instead of the duplicate failure-path
application through GetWriteFD; restore acquired saved state after attempted
application rather than setting echo=true. An acquired outer Restore remains
present even if cancellation prevents all set attempts, in which case it is
inert. Reuse the shared owned wait/cancellation lifetime; distinguish source
ENOTTY from infrastructure and refuse fallback after failed teardown. Preserve
UTF-8/no-readconv candidate consumption at the actual Go fill boundary using
Go's standard-library classification, without copied Unicode tables. No
arbitrary Ruby encoding/read-conversion, native buffering, configured
cfmakeraw, signal/job-control or successful restoration guarantee is claimed.
The existing ui prompt owns editing/output and has its own HighLine notice.

